.TH MAGNOLIE-ORGANIZER 1 "August 2026" "Magnolie Organizer 2.0.13" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
magnolie-organizer \- personal organizer in a classic paper design
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B magnolie-organizer
.RI [ option ]
.RI [ \-\-sprache\  language ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Magnolie Organizer
combines a calendar, tasks, contacts, notes, anniversaries and a yearly
planner. Data is stored locally and can optionally be synchronized through
Evolution Data Server or shared through the encrypted Magnolienbaum service.
.PP
Only one graphical instance is opened per user session. Starting the command
again presents the existing window, including a window hidden in the tray.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-erinnerung
Check for due reminders. This option is normally used by the session service.
.TP
.B \-\-wecker
Run the reminder monitor in the background.
.TP
.B \-\-tray-start
Start the organizer through its tray autostart entry.
.TP
.B \-\-probe
Test reminders and print a diagnostic report.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Continue normal operation while writing private, rotating startup, session,
singleton, window and tray diagnostics to
\fB~/.local/state/magnolie-organizer/debug.log\fR. Quit an already running
instance before starting a diagnostic run; a second invocation only activates
the existing process.
.TP
.BR \-\-sprache " " CODE , " " \-\-language " " CODE
Use a supported language code (\fBar\fR, \fBbe\fR, \fBcs\fR, \fBda\fR,
\fBde\fR, \fBen\fR, \fBes\fR, \fBfr\fR, \fBhi\fR, \fBhsb\fR, \fBit\fR,
\fBja\fR, \fBnb\fR, \fBnl\fR, \fBpl\fR, \fBpt\fR, \fBru\fR, \fBtr\fR,
\fBuk\fR, or \fBzh_CN\fR), or the system language (\fBsystem\fR) for this
invocation. This selects command output before help,
diagnostic and background modes and the WebKit interface of a newly opened
graphical instance. Persisted settings are not changed.
.TP
.BR \-\-pot " [" DATEI "]", " " \-\-pot-template " [" FILE "]"
Generate a reproducible gettext template and exit. With no file argument,
write \fBmagnolie-organizer.pot\fR in the current directory; otherwise write
to the specified path. The absolute output path is printed on success.
.TP
.BR \-\-hilfe , " " \-\-help
Show a short command overview.
.SH MAGNOLIENBAUM NETWORK
When enabled, Magnolienbaum listens on TCP port 8737 over IPv4 and IPv6.
Local branches are advertised and found through mDNS/DNS-SD as
\fB_magnolie._tcp.local.\fR. UDP port 8737 remains available as a
limited discovery fallback for older versions; UDP port 5353 is used by mDNS.
.PP
A host name, IPv4 address or IPv6 address can also be entered manually.
Pairing files accept reachable IPv4 and IPv6 literals. IPv6 brackets required
by URLs are added automatically and must not be stored in pairing files.
.SH WEATHER PRIVACY
The optional forecast sends requests to \fBwttr.in\fR. It first uses the
location in the user's address, then locally read LibreOffice user data. If
neither contains a location, wttr.in can estimate it from the public IP address
visible to the service. The calendar option “Do not retrieve weather without a
location” prevents any weather network request in that case.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/magnolie-organizer/
User data, settings, backups and reminder state.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/magnolie-organizer-tray.desktop
Optional tray autostart entry.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/magnolie-organizer/debug.log
Owner-only diagnostic log created when \fB\-\-debug\fR is used.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MAGNOLIE_ORGANIZER_WEB
Use an alternative directory containing the web interface. Intended for
development and testing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR magnolie-handbuch (1)
